When you execute:

sudo systemctl enable bootcamp-logger

systemd looks at:

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target

and creates an appropriate symlink under the target's .wants directory.

Conceptually:

/etc/systemd/system/
       │
       └── multi-user.target.wants/
                │
                └── bootcamp-logger.service → ../bootcamp-logger.service

So now:

multi-user.target
       │
       └── wants
             ↓
     bootcamp-logger.service

That's the magic behind WantedBy.

You can actually inspect it:

ls -l /etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/

You may see:

bootcamp-logger.service -> /etc/systemd/system/bootcamp-logger.service




